# `railway up` uploads this directory and HONORS this file, so anything listed
# here is absent from the deployed image as well as the build context. That cuts
# both ways: an earlier untracked .dockerignore listing two CSVs kept them out of
# production while git showed them present, and the file — not git — was the gate.
#
# So: only paths the running app provably does not read belong here. Never add
# anything under data/ — the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` is how the CSVs reach the
# image, and the site serves them at runtime.

# 260M of history. Nothing at runtime reads it; the only subprocess call in
# app.py is commented out. Halves a ~542M upload that was timing out.
.git

.cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
